course: dictionary
lesson: 11067
title: Weight: more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Weight means how heavy something is. We can measure it in grams, kilograms, ounces or pounds. «Your dose depends on your age and weight, which is why yours differs from your little sister's.» Here weight means how heavy a person is, and that is why doctors need to know it.
explain: Weight can also mean a heavy object, like a metal block on a scale or one lifted at the gym. «An anchor is a heavy shaped hook... the weight of its chain helps hold the ship» uses weight to mean how heavy the chain is. Read the words around the word to find which meaning fits.
explain: In science, weight is the pull of gravity on something. «A weight off my mind» is different: it is a phrase, and it means a worry has gone. When you are not sure, swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Weight means how heavy something is, and we measure it in grams, kilograms, ounces or pounds.
fact: A weight is a heavy object, like a metal block used on a scale or lifted for exercise.
fact: In science, weight is the pull of gravity on something.
fact: On the Moon you weigh less, but your mass stays the same.
fact: «A weight off my mind» means a worry has gone.
exercise: «Your dose depends on your age and weight.» What does weight mean here? | How tall someone is | How fast someone can run | How old someone is | *How heavy someone is
exercise: In science, what is weight? | The space something takes up | *The pull of gravity on something | The speed of a falling object | A kind of metal block
exercise: «A weight off my mind» means: | A heavy box carried upstairs | *A worry has gone | Someone has put on weight | A new kind of kitchen scale
test: Which unit is used to measure weight? | Litres | Seconds | *Kilograms | Metres
test: On the Moon, what changes about you? | Your mass goes up | Your height | Your shoe size | *Your weight is less
exam: Which word means the pull of gravity on something? | *Weight | Colour | Height | Speed
